      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The heart cycle comprises two main phases:\r\n\r\nDiastole: During diastole,
    the heart muscles relax, allowing the atria and then the ventricles to fill with
    blood from the pulmonary and systemic circuits.\r\n\r\nSystole: In systole, the
    heart contracts, first with the atria pushing blood into the ventricles, followed
    by the ventricles pumping blood out to the lungs (via the pulmonary artery) and
    the rest of the body (via the aorta).\r\n\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
